BIT-05: Fewer, cheaper interpreter dispatches

After caching, most of the time is the interpreter's dispatch, one per
token. Merge a number or variable operand into the operator that uses it,
evaluate each set of expressions as one program, jump directly from one
operation to the next, and rewrite expressions into equivalent forms that
need fewer operations and give the same bits.

Requires: none
Results: identical (every concentration, the output file and the report are unchanged)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, after FIX-01, FIX-02 and BIT-01 to BIT-04:
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn BIT-05.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

